* text=auto eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf

# ts-rs (frontend/types/rpc/*.ts, scripts/check-rpc-bindings.sh) emits
# trailing whitespace after any struct field that isn't the file's last —
# e.g. `message_id?: string, ` before the next field's doc comment. That's
# the generator's own formatting, not something this repo controls or a
# human introduced, and check-rpc-bindings.sh already enforces the real
# invariant (committed content byte-matches a fresh regeneration). Without
# this, `.githooks/pre-commit`'s `git diff --check` (whose actual job is
# catching unresolved merge-conflict markers, using git's whitespace check
# as the existing mechanism) blocks any commit that happens to move a
# previously-last field to a middle position, since that's the only time a
# trailing-whitespace line is "newly added" rather than pre-existing
# unchanged context. Confirmed other generated types (e.g.
# BackgroundTaskView.ts) already carry the same pattern undetected, simply
# because no prior PR's diff touched one of those lines directly.
frontend/types/rpc/*.ts -whitespace
